# Portfolio Configuration
# Single source of truth for portfolio definitions
# This file is a list of portfolios that will be synced to the database.
# The 'id' here is the primary key that will be used in the database.
#
# NOTE: base_currency is now defined globally in app_config.yaml
#       All portfolios use the same base currency for consistency
#
# Field Definitions:
# ------------------
# update_method:
#   - "automatic": Transactions are auto-synced from external APIs (IBKR, Binance.com, Binance.th, crypto wallets)
#                  Portfolio is included in automatic position reconciliation AND daily snapshots
#                  Used for: Securities, crypto (exchange & wallets), auto-synced broker cash
#
#   - "manual":    Transactions are entered manually (e.g., monthly cash updates, physical gold)
#                  Portfolio is EXCLUDED from both position reconciliation AND daily snapshots
#                  Used for: Cash holdings updated monthly, infrequently-traded assets
#                  Rationale: Avoid snapshot noise from stale data; snapshots created manually when updated
#
# status:
#   - "active":  Portfolio is currently operational
#                Behavior depends on update_method (see above)
#
#   - "closed":  Portfolio is inactive/historical (no new transactions)
#                Excluded from both position reconciliation AND daily snapshots
#                Used for: Deprecated portfolios, closed accounts
#
# Implementation:
# ---------------
# See service/portfolio_service.py:
# - reconcile_all_positions(): Excludes status='closed' OR update_method='manual'
# - create_all_snapshots():    Excludes status='closed' OR update_method='manual'
#
# Both automatic operations (reconciliation + snapshots) respect these flags to avoid
# processing portfolios that don't have fresh data or are no longer active.

# Example portfolios - customize for your setup
# Replace these with your actual portfolios

